course: dictionary
lesson: 11898
title: Browsing: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning depending on where you meet them. «Browsing» is one of these words. When you see it, read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Lara spent ages browsing the shelves in the library.» The shelves are a clue: she was looking through books in a relaxed way, not searching for one special book.
explain: «Sam was browsing the web for pictures of volcanoes.» Here the clue is the web. Browsing on the internet means looking at pages online. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then test your meaning. Does «Sam was looking at pages on the internet for pictures of volcanoes» still make sense? It does, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: In science, browsing means something different. «The giraffe was browsing on the leaves at the top of the tree.» Animals that browse eat leaves and twigs from bushes and trees. Cows are different: they graze, which means eating grass.
fact: Browse is a verb, and browsing is one of its forms: browse, browses, browsed, browsing.
fact: «Browsing» can mean looking through things in a relaxed way without searching for anything special, as in shops or books.
fact: «Browsing» can mean looking at pages on the internet, using a web browser such as Chrome, Safari or Firefox.
fact: «Browsing» can also describe animals, like giraffes and deer, eating leaves and twigs from bushes and trees.
fact: Online safety tip: browse safe sites, and tell an adult if you see something that upsets you.
exercise: «Mia spent an hour browsing the shelves in the library, but she did not pick a book.» What does browsing mean here? | Writing a long story | *Looking through things in a relaxed way, without searching for anything special | Running fast around the shelves | Cleaning the shelves
exercise: «Sam was browsing the web for pictures of volcanoes.» What is Sam doing? | *Looking at pages on the internet | Buying new shoes in a shop | Eating leaves from a tree | Reading a paper map
exercise: Which animal is a browser, one that eats leaves and twigs from trees? | Cow | *Giraffe | Goldfish
test: Tom says, «Browse safe sites, and tell an adult if you see something upsetting.» What does browse mean in this sentence? | Eating snacks while sitting down | Sleeping under a blanket | Drawing pictures on paper | *Looking at websites on a computer
test: In a shop, someone says, «Oh, I'm just browsing.» What do they mean? | *They are looking around without buying anything special yet | They are wrapping a present | They are running a race | They are stealing something
exam: Which sentence uses browsing with the meaning of looking at web pages? | «The cows were grazing in the field.» | *«Ella was browsing for dinosaur facts online.» | «Ben was browsing the shelves for a new comic.» | «The deer were browsing on the leaves.»
